{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1362646-canon-fan-splat-characters-in-mortal-kombat-11","id":1362646,"title":"Canon/Fan Splat Characters in Mortal Kombat 11","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-22T07:54:30-08:00","id":1362646,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Canon/Fan Splat Characters in Mortal Kombat 11","content":"Essentially what it says in a tin; if you could create a Character for MK11 of one of the various Splats (both 'Canonical' (made by White Wolf and produced by Onyx Path Productions) and 'Homebrew' (made by the fans, for the fans (and anyone else who's interested.).),), what would they be like to play as? What would their Fatal Blow, Fatalities, Brutalities, Intro and Victory Cinematics, pre-fight Banter, Tower Ending, etc, etc, be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 01-23-2020, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T09:49:09-08:00","id":1363647,"title":"","content":"Hm. I'm no fighting game fan, but I have an idea for the leader of the Synod of Seeking, the Jeremiad group who serves as the viewpoint characters when I'm Let's Reading:<br /> <br /> <b>Neferyah, Wandering Sage of Irem</b>:<br /> <br /> <b>Intro: </b>The short intro involves her sarcophagus exploding at the spell of her cultist and reforming into armor. Long intro is her lowering onto the field on a golden, technomagical throne as she talks with her opponent, then hopping to her feet as it vanishes.<br /> <br /> <b>Cetrion Dialogue:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Neferyah: </b>A fellow goddess, I assume?<br /> <br /> <b>Cetrion: </b>You flatter yourself, creation of the exiles.<br /> <br /> <b>Neferyah: </b>You assume that's a compliment, creation of Kronika.<br /> <br /> <b>Raiden Dialogue:<br /> <br /> Raiden: </b>Your people were our mistake.<br /> <br /> <b>Neferyah: </b>And punishment follows hubris.<br /> <br /> <b>Raiden: </b>As you will soon discover.<br /> <br /> <b>Playstyle: </b>Puppet fighter, uses a robed cultist as a frequent assist character. Her personal weapon is a pair of large bronze knives she uses as a shortranged weapon, but mostly to direct her cultists around.<br /> <br /> <b>Victory Cinematic: </b>Wets her knives with the opponent's blood, then calls out her throne to take her to the council chamber of the Synod of Seeking, where she stands before a room of cheering cultists as she flicks it into a sacrificial fire in front of an altar to Neheb-Ka.<br /> <br /> <b>Fatality</b>:<br /> <br /> <i>Mother of Idols: </i>Neferyah whistles to her cultist, who tackles her opponent to the ground as she gestures with her knives offscreen. A large cauldron of boiling metal is wheeled in, and she spears her opponent with her knives and tosses them in. As the opponent burns and sinks, she carries in a large statue of Neheb-Ka and, after the bronzed opponent is poured out of the cauldron, she positions it so that the Judge is stepping in her opponents' face. She nods respectfully to it as the cultist kneels.<br /> <br /> <i>Instructive Moment: </i>Neferyah gestures to her cultist to pull out a notepad, and he sits on a much less ornate chair as she slowly starts dismembering her opponent, stopping frequently to see if the cultist is taking notes. Eventually, she is left with nothing but a hand, and she goes over to check on his work. She then cuts open the finger of the hand to serve as a grading pen, giving him a B+. The notepad, naturally, has a bunch of in-jokes on it, and morbid black comedy.<br /> <br /> <b>Tower Ending: </b>&quot;I pity Kronika, to be frank. I was a mortal before I was a god, and she was a Titan, without even peers to assuage her loneliness. I do not blame her; I blame the power she had, this Relic she called her hourglass. The one thing it has that I do not is perception and history - and perception and history are the only things I desire. I take a full record of my past, and make my only alteration; that someone finds the complete history of Irem, and with it, that my Kin of the Lightened Soul have all the records they need to prove they are its heirs. Soon, I will return to the Judges, and I will take the hourglass with me, far, far away from where anyone will use it again - and when I return, I know from my future, that I will return to a world where the Kin have become the ideological guides of a world where the founding principle is not laws, but Ma'at, and they will not have summoned me - because they will not have needed me. The world I come to is one where I am not a god, but a strange woman out of time. In my future, I am free.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T12:02:28-08:00","id":1363834,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the post! But just to clarify, since you evidently aren\u2019t familiar with the game itself, characters in MK11 (which is the sole game we\u2019re focusing on in this thread, because I have the most familiarity with it) don\u2019t have a short intro or long intro, but four different intro cinematics, along with four (five in Scorpion\u2019s and Sub-Zero's cases) cinematic victory animations.<br /> <br /> The former, of course, always comes about at the start of the fight, albeit randomly if more than one is equipped. The latter, meanwhile, only triggers under one of two conditions; 1) You strike the enemy Kombatant with anything other than a Fatality or Deux) the Fatality Timer runs out (at which point the opponent just keels over). And some moves can trigger a Brutality if you have it unlocked, certain conditions are met during the match (I.e. never losing a round, or initiating it on the Final Round) and the move depletes the other character\u2019s health to 0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 02-15-2020, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T09:02:28-08:00","id":1364169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1362646-canon-fan-splat-characters-in-mortal-kombat-11?p=1363647#post1363647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Neferyah, Wandering Sage of Irem</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Now, that is awesome. From the intros through the dialogue and especially the Tower ending, that is a lot of personality you've managed to show there. I find the issue with this sort of thought experiment (which I may or may not engage in with frightening regularity) is the vast difference between CofD's (to me seeming) far more subtle and subdued themes and things like MK11's far more flashy and colourful expressions, but I feel that you nailed it. For Brutalities, I could see an attack with the knives impaling her opponent before Neferyah summons a brazier of sacrificial fire and flings them in, as well as a cultist attack turning into a pile-on as more and more nondescript hooded figures jump on top of the opponent, the ending being Neferyah doing her victory pose next to a literal pile of bodies as tall as herself. Also, depending on her relationship to her cult, she could 'block' by using a cultist as a human shield, or they fling themselves in between her and the incoming harm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24688-mrmeow","name":"MrMeow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T15:31:13-08:00","id":1364238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMeow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1362646-canon-fan-splat-characters-in-mortal-kombat-11?p=1364169#post1364169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the issue with this sort of thought experiment (which I may or may not engage in with frightening regularity) is the vast difference between CofD's (to me seeming) far more subtle and subdued themes and things like MK11's far more flashy and colourful expressions, but I feel that you nailed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m wholly aware of the differences in presentation between the two, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24688-mrmeow\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24688\" data-vbnamecard=\"24688\">MrMeow</a>. But think of it like this; the power held by mid-to-high tier PCs and NPCs from CoD enables them to easily pull off the sorts of fights that the MK franchise is famous for if the ST allows it and the players are able to set things up correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 02-02-2020, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}